<section id="about" aria-labelledby="h-about"><div class="wrap">
  <h2 id="h-about">About</h2>
  <div style="max-width:660px">
    <p>I spent four years at Reliance Industries doing the unglamorous work that determines whether a manufacturing programme ships on time: negotiating with cell suppliers across ten countries, evaluating hundreds of vendor proposals, and chasing containers across three ports until they arrived.</p>
    <p>What I learned is that most commercial problems are not strategy problems. They are visibility problems. Nobody knows where the goods are, what they really cost, or which supplier is about to fail — and by the time anyone finds out, the decision has already been made for them.</p>
    <p>I moved to Leeds in September 2026 for my MBA because I want to apply that same discipline to consumer and retail businesses, where supply chain is not a back-office function but the thing that determines margin, markdown and whether a product exists at all.</p>
    <p>Outside work I am a certified Bharatanatyam dancer, a state-level tennis player, and I was elected class representative four years running — which, more than anything on my CV, is where I learned to get people to agree on a deadline.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:15px"><strong>Work authorisation:</strong> eligible for the UK Graduate (post-study work) route on completion of my MBA — no sponsorship required.</p>
